{"answer": "Here is a quote from the paper 'You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object Detection' by Joseph Redmon et al.:

"We present YOLO, a new approach to object detection. Prior work on object detection repurposes classifiers to perform detection. Instead, we frame object detection as a regression problem to spatially separated bounding boxes and associated class probabilities. A single neural network predicts bounding boxes and class probabilities directly from full images in one evaluation. Since the whole detection pipeline is a single network, it can be optimized end-to-end directly on detection performance."

Our unified architecture is extremely fast. Our base YOLO model processes images in real-time at 45 frames per second. A smaller version of the network, Fast YOLO, processes an astounding 155 frames per second while still achieving double the mAP of other real-time detectors.", "citations": [{"text": "Joseph Redmon, Ali Farhadi, Santosh Divvala, Ross Girshick. You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object Detection.", "section": "Abstract"}]}

